Title: COLD HANDOFF
Author: Rachel Stein
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. SAFE HOUSE - KITCHEN - NIGHT

Lena tapes a burner phone shut. A map marks three exchange points in red.
LENA
One hour. In and out. No second chances.

INT. PARKING GARAGE - LEVEL 4 - NIGHT

Rain. The BLACK DUFFEL at her feet. No courier.
LENA
Package is clean. Where's your courier?

INT. PARKING GARAGE - STAIRWELL - NIGHT

DMITRI VOLKOV limps into view, bleeding.
DMITRI
They made me at the bridge.

INT. SILVER SUV - MOVING - NIGHT

Lena weaves through traffic. Headlights follow.
DMITRI
If they take this back, a city dies tomorrow.

INT. UNDERPASS - NIGHT

Lena kills the lights, coasts into darkness. The sedan overshoots.
LENA
We have four minutes before they circle back.

EXT. RIVER ROAD OVERPASS - NIGHT

Lena pries open a maintenance hatch. Sirens distant.
LENA
Dmitri goes in the hatch. I draw the tail.

INT. SILVER SUV - NIGHT

The sedan rams them. Lena's knuckles white on the wheel.
DMITRI
I'm not leaving you with them.
LENA
You're leaving with the film. That's the job.

EXT. OVERPASS GUARDRAIL - NIGHT

Dmitri drops into the hatch. Lena slams the SUV into reverse.
LENA
Go.

INT. SILVER SUV - NIGHT

Three men exit the sedan — armed, professional. Lena smiles without warmth.
LENA
You want the package? Come get it.

EXT. RIVER ROAD OVERPASS - NIGHT

She accelerates toward the gap between sedan and rail. The duffel is gone. The city, for tonight, is not.
LENA
Let's see who's still standing when the rain stops.

FADE OUT.


THE END
